<title>NETHERLANDS: KNP BT to cut jobs at cardboard unit.</title>
<headline>KNP BT to cut jobs at cardboard unit.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch paper and packaging group NV Koninklijke KNP BT said on Wednesday it had reached agreement with unions on a reorganisation of its cardboard plants in the northern Netherlands.</p>
<p>About 120 jobs of a total 1,090 will be cut as part of a restructuring announced last year, spokesman Patrick de Leede told Reuters.</p>
<p>KNP BT will try to prevent forced dismissals by transferring employees to other production sites in this part of the country and by offering a premium to employees who resign, he added.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
